From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vkd3d: Feature level 12_0 with tiled resources tier 1.

The PS5's RADV binds sparse resources but has no PRT, so vkd3d-proton
reports tiled resources tier 1, and feature level 12_0 asks for tier 2:
the device stopped at 11_1, and games that need 12_0 (Unreal Engine 5's)
refused to start. 12_0 is now given with tier 1. The tier reported stays
1, so a game that checks it for tier 2's residency feedback doesn't use
it.
---
 libs/vkd3d/device.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/device.c b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
index 63a82c3..4a630ff 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/device.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
@@ -9729,8 +9729,12 @@ static void d3d12_device_caps_init_feature_level(struct d3d12_device *device)
             vk_info->device_limits.maxPerStageDescriptorStorageImages >= D3D12_UAV_SLOT_COUNT)
         caps->max_feature_level = D3D_FEATURE_LEVEL_11_1;
 
+    /* PC5: 12_0 with tiled resources tier 1, which the PS5's RADV gives: it binds
+     * sparse resources but has no PRT, so no residency feedback (tier 2's). The tier
+     * reported stays 1, so games that check it for tier 2 features don't use them,
+     * and games that need 12_0 (Unreal Engine 5's, among others) start. */
     if (caps->max_feature_level >= D3D_FEATURE_LEVEL_11_1 &&
-            caps->options.TiledResourcesTier >= D3D12_TILED_RESOURCES_TIER_2 &&
+            caps->options.TiledResourcesTier >= D3D12_TILED_RESOURCES_TIER_1 &&
             caps->options.ResourceBindingTier >= D3D12_RESOURCE_BINDING_TIER_2 &&
             caps->options.TypedUAVLoadAdditionalFormats)
         caps->max_feature_level = D3D_FEATURE_LEVEL_12_0;
